{"id":128,"number":66,"symbol":"Clat","name":"Clathrin heavy chain 1","gene":"CLTC","family":"STR","location":"E","other_locations":[],"cell_rank":0,"mass_kda":191.6,"length_aa":1675,"discovery_year":1975,"milestone":"Clathrin named as the coat protein of vesicles (Pearse)","blurb":"Three-legged triskelion that builds cages around budding vesicles.","drugs":[],"therapeutic":null,"pathways":[],"orthologs":{"ecoli":null,"human":"CLTC","mouse":"Cltc","yeast":"CHC1"},"variant_count":0,"misfolded":null,"uniprot_id":"Q00610","function":"Clathrin is the major protein of the polyhedral coat of coated pits and vesicles. Two different adapter protein complexes link the clathrin lattice either to the plasma membrane or to the trans-Golgi network. Acts as a component of the TACC3/ch-TOG/clathrin complex proposed to contribute to stabilization of kinetochore fibers of the mitotic spindle by acting as inter-microtubule bridge. The TACC3/ch-TOG/clathrin complex is required for the maintenance of kinetochore fiber tension. Plays a role in early autophagosome formation. Interaction with DNAJC6 mediates the recruitment of HSPA8 to the clathrin lattice and creates local destabilization of the lattice promoting uncoating","sequence":"","pdb_ids":["9C0Y","9C0Z","6E4L","4G55","2XZG","7BN1","7BN2","6QNN","7ZX4","6QNP"],"alphafold_url":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q00610-F1-model_v6.pdb","variants":[],"partners":[{"id":72,"symbol":"Adb2","name":"Beta-2 adrenergic receptor","score":0.905,"effect_out":null,"effect_in":null},{"id":127,"symbol":"Tau","name":"Microtubule-associated protein tau","score":0.802,"effect_out":null,"effect_in":null},{"id":68,"symbol":"Egfr","name":"Epidermal growth factor receptor","score":0.759,"effect_out":null,"effect_in":null}]}